</div></div></div><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="ixhjtwi"><img id="fkt-image-ce3-486-893" title="" target="_self" src="{{ 'ageaura-f6-02.webp' | asset_url }}" href="" align="center" alt="" onclick="" style="width:100%!important;height:auto!important;object-fit:contain!important;aspect-ratio:auto!important;max-height:none!important;" class="fk-image-defaults" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="ih8f78"><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-ASKCcEx7Klw3">Dear Friend Worried About Aging,&nbsp; If you're reading this with that quiet, creeping suspicion that something has shifted in your body over the last few years — the stiffness when you stand up, the afternoon fog that didn't used to be there, the face in the mirror that looks like it's <em>settling in</em> instead of still building — I want you to stop scrolling for a moment.<br><br> I almost didn't write this letter.<br><br> As a longevity doctor with twenty-six years in translational biology, I am careful about what I put my name to.<br><br> But what I have watched happen in my own clinic over the last fourteen months, in the bloodwork of patients I have personally followed back from Shanghai, is something I cannot in good conscience keep quiet about.<br><br> So I'm going to tell you what I saw, what it means, and exactly what to do with this information — if you have the courage to actually act on it.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i5sihc"><h3 style="margin:44px 0 20px;padding:0 12px;">THE PHONE CALL THAT CHANGED EVERYTHING I THOUGHT I KNEW ABOUT AGING…</h3></div><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="itcqk86"><img id="fkt-image-8f3-da0-9f5" title="" target="_self" src="{{ 'ageaura-f6-03.webp' | asset_url }}" href="" align="center" alt="" width="" height="" onclick="" style="width:100%!important;height:auto!important;object-fit:contain!important;aspect-ratio:auto!important;max-height:none!important;" class="fk-image-defaults disable-fk-lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="ijc1c58" class="d-none"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="if6ohwg" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><img src="{{ 'ageaura-f6-04.webp' | asset_url }}" id="i8ivigl" style="position:static!important;width:100%!important;height:auto!important;object-fit:contain!important;aspect-ratio:auto!important;max-height:none!important;" class="fk-i4vh35o embed-responsive-item fk-disable-lazy" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i2700n">It happened on a Tuesday afternoon.<br><br> I had just finished rounds when my phone rang.<br><br> It was James Calloway — a longtime patient, sixty-four years old, retired managing partner of one of the largest private equity firms in the Northeast.<br><br> James is the kind of man who plays squash four mornings a week, reads three medical journals for fun, and has never once missed his annual executive physical.<br><br> He is also the kind of man who does not call his doctor in the middle of the day unless something is wrong.<br><br> "Marcus," he said, "I need you to look at my numbers.<br><br> I just got back from Shanghai." I almost laughed.<br><br> "James, why on Earth were you in Shanghai?" "Because," he said, "two of my partners have been going for the last eight months.<br><br> And Marcus — they don't look the same anymore.<br><br> I'm not talking about a tan.<br><br> I'm talking about the way their skin sits on their face.<br><br> The way they get out of a chair.<br><br> Last weekend I watched Bill — he's sixty-eight — beat his thirty-five-year-old son in straight sets.<br><br> I have known Bill for twenty-two years.<br><br> The man couldn't climb a flight of stairs without complaining about his knee last year." That was the call.<br><br> A week later, James was sitting in my office sliding a manila envelope across my desk.<br><br> Inside was a TruDiagnostic epigenetic panel — baseline, and again ninety days later.<br><br> His biological age had dropped from <strong>71.2 to 34.6</strong>.<br><br> Thirty-six and a half years.<br><br> In ninety days.<br><br> I have been doing this for a long time.<br><br> I have never seen numbers move like that.<br><br> I picked up the phone and started making my own calls.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="ira3zeb"><h3 style="margin:44px 0 20px;padding:0 12px;">WHY THE WEALTHIEST PEOPLE ON EARTH ARE QUIETLY FLYING TO SHANGHAI</h3></div><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="i6iuzyf"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="im9ylgj" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><img src="{{ 'ageaura-f6-05.webp' | asset_url }}" id="ir4elzu" style="position:static!important;width:100%!important;height:auto!important;object-fit:contain!important;aspect-ratio:auto!important;max-height:none!important;" class="fk-i4vh35o embed-responsive-item disable-fk-lazy" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-Oh1MW2aFlH8e">For five months I became a man possessed.<br><br> I cancelled speaking engagements.<br><br> I read every available paper out of the Shanghai Institute of Biochemistry and Cell Biology, the Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, and the longevity divisions attached to Fudan and ShanghaiTech Universities.<br><br> I personally reviewed labs, bloodwork, epigenetic clocks, inflammatory panels, and cardiac scans from seventeen patients who had gone through the Shanghai protocol.<br><br> The pattern was no longer deniable.<br><br> The Chinese government has poured a staggering amount of capital into translational longevity science over the last fifteen years — and unlike in the United States, where the field is fragmented across hundreds of competing private startups, Shanghai's major research institutions operate in coordinated clusters.<br><br> They share data.<br><br> They share results.<br><br> They run human trials at a speed that is simply not possible under the current FDA framework.<br><br> Bryan Johnson — the man spending two million dollars a year on his Blueprint protocol — has publicly admitted the most advanced peptide work on Earth is being done in Shanghai.<br><br> Peter Attia has referenced it.<br><br> So has David Sinclair.<br><br> They just don't say it on television.<br><br> That is why people who can afford a sixteen-hour flight on a private jet are taking it.<br><br> And what they figured out — the genuinely important part — is that aging is not <em>one</em> process.<br><br> It is at least twelve distinct biological processes happening at the same time, falling into three categories that must be addressed <strong>simultaneously, in sequence, with three different classes of compounds</strong>.</div><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="ivek8a3"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="ivbhnc9" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-1by1"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0810/1563/6283/files/3_layer.webp?v=1781006925" id="irxowjf" style="position:static!important;width:100%!important;height:auto!important;object-fit:contain!important;aspect-ratio:auto!important;max-height:none!important;" class="fk-i4vh35o embed-responsive-item disable-fk-lazy" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i0lyhj">Think of your body as a precision machine that has been running on three failing systems at once.<br><br> By age forty, your <strong>mitochondria</strong> — the energy factories inside every cell — start piling up damaged units faster than your body can recycle them.<br><br> The process that clears them out, called <em>mitophagy</em>, slows to a crawl.<br><br> Energy drops.<br><br> Inflammation rises.<br><br> Recovery takes weeks instead of days.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="izziuxk">By 50, your <strong>NAD+</strong> levels — the molecular fuel that powers more than five hundred enzymatic reactions, including every single DNA-repair pathway you have — are roughly half what they were at twenty.<br><br> Your sirtuins (the so-called longevity genes) literally cannot function without NAD+.<br><br> The repair crews are still on payroll.<br><br> They just have nothing left to work with.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="iwb56zw">By 60, your <strong>peptide signaling</strong> — the precise messengers that tell your tissues to repair, rebuild, and stay structurally strong — has collapsed.<br><br> Sleep architecture falls apart.<br><br> Collagen synthesis crawls.<br><br> Wounds that healed in three days at thirty now take three weeks.<br><br> The body forgets how to be young.</div><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="imzww3"><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="iywxt7j"><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="is3wg4d">The longevity research community has known this since the 2013 Lopez-Otin paper <em>The Hallmarks of Aging</em> — the single most-cited paper in the field.<br><br> Every supplement, drug, and protocol marketed to aging Americans over the last thirty years has tried to target <strong>one</strong> of these hallmarks at a time.<br><br> NAD+ boosters.<br><br> Resveratrol.<br><br> Senolytics.<br><br> Each one good at one thing.<br><br> None of them addressing the full picture.<br><br> The Shanghai clusters figured out that you have to hit all three layers — mitochondrial cleanup, NAD+ restoration, peptide signaling — at the same time.<br><br> That is the discovery.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i1dnu3j"><h3 style="margin:44px 0 20px;padding:0 12px;">WHY EVERYTHING YOU'VE TRIED HAS QUIETLY FAILED</h3></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="why-intro-v19">I have prescribed and reviewed every major longevity intervention available in the United States for the last decade.<br><br> Let me dismantle the single-compound options you have probably tried — and explain why none of them, on their own, has ever moved the needle for you the way the field promised they would.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="isdenzf"><strong>NMN alone.<br><br></strong> Yes, it raises NAD+.<br><br> But taken without a methyl donor like TMG, it slowly depletes your methylation pathway, drives up homocysteine, and quietly costs you elsewhere.<br><br> Most NMN brands on Amazon are also under-dosed by 60-70%.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="il8dax5"><strong>Resveratrol.<br><br></strong> The Sinclair-era darling.<br><br> Almost no clinically meaningful effect in humans without active sirtuin substrate (NAD+).<br><br> It is the spark with no fuel — sold by the millions of bottles to people who never get the second compound.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="it6rayw"><strong>Standard testosterone replacement.<br><br></strong> Expensive — $200–400/month — and it addresses exactly one hormone while doing nothing for the underlying mitochondrial, NAD+, and peptide-signaling collapse driving the symptoms in the first place.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="inmbvb9-couples"><strong>Concierge longevity clinics.</strong> $30,000 to $100,000 per year.<br><br> Marble lobbies, extensive labs, identical underlying protocol.<br><br> The science they are delivering is real.<br><br> The markup is the building you are sitting in.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="inmbvb9-natural"><strong>"Anti-aging" supplements off Amazon.<br><br></strong> Astragalus.<br><br> Spermidine.<br><br> Berberine.<br><br> Most are under-dosed by an order of magnitude.<br><br> None of them address all three layers of the aging process.<br><br> You are paying for the label, not the compound.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="inmbvb9-summary">Every one of these treats a single mechanism while ignoring the other two layers that are still failing.<br><br> That is why nothing has worked.<br><br> That is why your blood markers have not moved.<br><br> That is why the mirror keeps telling the same story.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="ikfy6ba"><h3 style="margin:44px 0 20px;padding:0 12px;">THE 3-COMPOUND PROTOCOL HIDING IN PLAIN SIGHT</h3></div><div data-secondsdelay="" id="i9h53o6" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><img src="{{ 'ageaura-f6-07.webp' | asset_url }}" id="il9jsjw" style="position:static!important;width:100%!important;height:auto!important;object-fit:contain!important;aspect-ratio:auto!important;max-height:none!important;" class="fk-i4vh35o embed-responsive-item disable-fk-lazy" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-tGUN1ZootH6a">Remember James?<br><br> Six weeks after I put him on the full three-layer Shanghai protocol, his wife noticed before he did.<br><br> She told him at breakfast that the texture of his skin had changed.<br><br> He looked in the mirror three times before he saw it himself.<br><br> Day ninety: biological age 34.6.<br><br> CRP 0.8.<br><br> VO2 max 41.2.<br><br> Resting heart rate 58.<br><br> His cardiologist — a colleague of mine at Mass General — called me directly and asked me to put his wife on it.<br><br> The protocol is three compounds.<br><br> Each one targets a different one of the three aging layers.<br><br> Each one is dosed at the exact level the clinical literature actually demands.<br><br> And each one is useless without the other two.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i99fgx9"><h4 style="margin:28px 0 12px;padding:0;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:800;line-height:1.3;color:#0a0a0a;">1. AgeAura Pure Urolithin A — the Mitophagy Activator.</h4> The only compound ever proven in a Nature Metabolism human trial to directly activate mitochondrial recycling.<br><br> Cleans damaged mitochondria out of your cells the way your body did at thirty. <strong>500 mg clinical dose</strong> — not the 100-250 mg cosmetic doses you see on Amazon.<br><br> This is Layer 1: you cannot rebuild a cell that has not first been cleaned.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i7dflus"><h4 style="margin:28px 0 12px;padding:0;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:800;line-height:1.3;color:#0a0a0a;">2. AgeAura Pure NMN + TMG — the NAD+ Restoration Pair.</h4> Clinical-dose NMN pre-paired with trimethylglycine — the methyl donor that lets NMN raise NAD+ <em>without</em> taxing your methylation pathway elsewhere.<br><br> Take NMN alone and you are running a hidden tax.<br><br> Take them together, the way Shanghai does, and you raise NAD+ cleanly.<br><br> This is Layer 2: the fuel for every repair you have left.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i7dflus-b"><h4 style="margin:28px 0 12px;padding:0;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:800;line-height:1.3;color:#0a0a0a;">3. AgeAura Pure Longevity Peptides — the Signaling Layer.</h4> A pharmaceutical-grade peptide complex sourced from the same manufacturer that supplies several Shanghai clinical programs.<br><br> Tells your body, at the molecular level, to start behaving the way it did fifteen years ago.<br><br> Sleep deepens.<br><br> Recovery accelerates.<br><br> Skin elasticity returns.<br><br> Lean tissue rebuilds.<br><br> Miss even one layer and you stay stuck.<br><br> That is why every single-compound product on the market has failed you.<br><br> That is why the full protocol works.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-J0TkJtWE0lu0"><h3 style="margin:44px 0 20px;padding:0 12px;">WORD SPREAD INSIDE THE FIELD</h3></div><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="ikrobdu"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="iy59m94" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><img src="{{ 'ageaura-f6-08.webp' | asset_url }}" id="ic97xxa" style="position:static!important;width:100%!important;height:auto!important;object-fit:contain!important;aspect-ratio:auto!important;max-height:none!important;" class="fk-i4vh35o embed-responsive-item disable-fk-lazy" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-Yev87gre1wCt">After James's panel came back, word got out the way it always does in a tight medical circle.<br><br> Slowly at first.<br><br> Then quickly.<br><br> Two cardiologists at Mass General asked me about it.<br><br> A peptide-therapy MD in New York flew up to review the data.<br><br> By month four I had patients flying in from Los Angeles, Miami, and Vancouver.<br><br> By month eight I was tracking roughly fourteen hundred patients on the same three-layer protocol — every one of them showing measurable biological-age reduction in their first ninety days.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-MVjB74x9W8ru"><h3 style="margin:44px 0 20px;padding:0 12px;">AND THEN THE PUSHBACK STARTED</h3></div><img title="" target="_self" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0810/1563/6283/files/protocol.webp?v=1781006925" href="" align="center" alt="" width="" height="" onclick="" id="fkt-image-dfd-da1-948" style="width:100%!important;height:auto!important;object-fit:contain!important;aspect-ratio:auto!important;max-height:none!important;" class="fk-image-defaults disable-fk-lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-tSh4Ox0XjtK7">First it was friendly.<br><br> A colleague I have known for eighteen years pulled me aside at a longevity-medicine conference and told me, kindly, that what I was describing was "going to make a lot of people uncomfortable." Then it was less friendly.<br><br> A polite letter from a supplement industry trade association suggesting I "reconsider how I framed my findings publicly." Then a regulatory body opened an inquiry — no findings, just an inquiry — that took six months to resolve.<br><br> The reason is obvious.<br><br> American supplement companies make their money selling you <em>one</em> compound at a time, at the lowest possible dose that can legally carry the name on the label.<br><br> American pharmaceutical companies cannot patent NMN.<br><br> They cannot patent Urolithin A.<br><br> They cannot patent naturally occurring peptide sequences.<br><br> There is nobody with a stock price who is incentivized to put this on the news.</div><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="iru1sew"><ul id="i25co5m" class="fk-bullet"><li id="iznddjl"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="iy0vtt8" class="fk-bullet-list-container bullet-list-container"><div data-secondsdelay="" class="fk-bullet-icon-container"><i id="imi45gq" class="icp icp-auto fas fa-circle">
				  </i></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="iqlkjvp">Addresses the ROOT CAUSE of biological aging (all three layers — not one at a time)</div></div></li><li id="izicd8g"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="iftxdki" class="fk-bullet-list-container bullet-list-container"><div data-secondsdelay="" class="fk-bullet-icon-container"><i id="idvq5rl" class="icp icp-auto fas fa-circle">
				  </i></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="ii3r4uv">Costs less than one month at any concierge longevity clinic</div></div></li><li id="ivbhehn"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="iuamajf" class="fk-bullet-list-container bullet-list-container"><div data-secondsdelay="" class="fk-bullet-icon-container"><i id="iwdruml" class="icp icp-auto fas fa-circle">
				  </i></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="iurma5d">Delivered to your door — no $200,000 Swiss retreat, no clinic membership fee</div></div></li></ul></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i45ftvo">But here is what the trade associations didn't count on… the patients getting their lives back weren't going to stay quiet.<br><br> They told their spouses.<br><br> They told their friends.<br><br> They told their cardiologists.<br><br> The information was moving faster than anyone could shut it down.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="itksswy"><h3 style="margin:44px 0 20px;padding:0 12px;">THE ONLY PROTOCOL THAT DELIVERS ALL THREE LAYERS</h3></div><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="i524twj"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="isyommj" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><img src="{{ 'ageaura-f6-10.webp' | asset_url }}" id="iyonet6" style="position:static!important;width:100%!important;height:auto!important;object-fit:contain!important;aspect-ratio:auto!important;max-height:none!important;" class="fk-i4vh35o embed-responsive-item disable-fk-lazy" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="ihljs5">It is called the <strong>AgeAura Pure Protocol</strong>.<br><br> Three pharmaceutical-grade compounds.<br><br> One daily ritual.<br><br> Clinical doses on every single ingredient.<br><br> Manufactured to the same specifications as the Shanghai-affiliated clinical programs.<br><br> Available without the flight.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-CD80XZ3eXphA"><h3 style="margin:44px 0 20px;padding:0 12px;">HERE'S EXACTLY WHAT HAPPENS INSIDE YOUR BODY</h3></div><div data-box="true" data-secondsdelay="" id="iaegt06"><div data-secondsdelay="" id="iuoimni" class="embed-responsive embed-responsive-16by9"><img src="{{ 'ageaura-f6-11.webp' | asset_url }}" id="inhc40w" style="position:static!important;width:100%!important;height:auto!important;object-fit:contain!important;aspect-ratio:auto!important;max-height:none!important;" class="fk-i4vh35o embed-responsive-item disable-fk-lazy" alt="" loading="lazy"></div></div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="i955kux"><strong>Days 1–7: The Mitophagy Awakening.<br><br></strong> Urolithin A activates the cellular recycling pathway that has been dormant since your forties.<br><br> Damaged mitochondria start clearing.<br><br> The first thing most patients report — including James — is that the afternoon energy crash simply does not happen anymore.<br><br> Deep sleep, measured on an Oura ring, climbs 12–18% within the first week. <strong>Days 8–28: The NAD+ Surge.<br><br></strong> NMN + TMG drives tissue NAD+ levels back up toward where they were in your thirties.<br><br> Mental clarity sharpens.<br><br> Inflammatory markers (CRP) typically drop by 50–60%.<br><br> Patients report being able to read at ten p.m.<br><br> "the way they could in their forties." Resting heart rate falls 8–12 beats. <strong>Days 29–60: The Peptide Rebuild.<br><br></strong> The Longevity Peptide complex takes over.<br><br> Visible change.<br><br> Skin texture shifts.<br><br> Jawline tightens.<br><br> Lean tissue gains begin, fat loss begins — without changing training or diet.<br><br> Spouses notice before patients do. <strong>Days 61–90: The Biological Age Drop.<br><br></strong> The full ninety-day panel — TruDiagnostic epigenetic clock, full inflammatory panel, VO2 max, sleep architecture — comes back showing measured biological age reduction of 12 to 36 years against baseline.<br><br> That is not exaggeration.<br><br> That is the average across roughly fourteen hundred patients I am now personally tracking.</div><div data-text="text" data-secondsdelay="" id="cc-id-tUFK9E1hWHo7"><h3 style="margin:44px 0 20px;padding:0 12px;">THE RESULTS SPEAK FOR THEMSELVES</h3></div><img title="" target="_self" src="{{ 'ageaura-f6-12.webp' | asset_url }}" href="" align="center" alt="" width="" height="" onclick=""